You were very close. To get the model you want use

m <- '
F1 = 1-10
F2 = 11-20
F3 = 21-30

COV = F1*F2, F1*F3, F2*F3'

model <- confmirt.model(m)
m1 <- mirt(data, model, itemtype='Rasch')

You also could have extracted and edited the starting values directly
by passing pars = 'values', editing the returned data.frame, and
putting it back into the function. Hope that helps.

Phil

P.S. Note that confmirt.model() will be replaced by mirt.model(), just
to save a future headache.

